      "<strong>v2.0.0 &mdash; Cross-Sell is whole: your own offers, and the win on every booking path (Patient-Profitability OS).</strong> The third revenue meter is now complete on both axes. <strong>(1) Author your own offers.</strong> Cross-sell is no longer manufacturer-only &mdash; on <strong>Recognition &rarr; Rewards</strong> there&rsquo;s now <em>&ldquo;Your own offers&rdquo;</em>: pick one of your services, set a dollar discount and an optional date window, and it badges that service at booking exactly like an Allergan promo &mdash; and earns the same <code>$5 cross_sell_addon</code> win when a matched patient books it. Spa-authored offers and manufacturer promos are <strong>peers in one pipeline</strong>: same table, same at-booking badge, same ledger. (A manufacturer-calendar re-upload now only replaces <em>its</em> offers and leaves yours untouched.) <strong>(2) The win fires on patient self-book too.</strong> Until now the <code>$5</code> cross-sell win recorded only when the <em>owner</em> booked; now it also fires when a <strong>patient books themselves</strong> on <code>/s/&lt;slug&gt;</code> &mdash; where most bookings actually happen. We snapshot the chosen service onto the held appointment so the two-phase hold&rarr;confirm flow can attribute it (which also backfills what every native booking was treated for). Still matched-only: <code>$5</code> only when the patient resolves in your book, and the booking never blocks on attribution. <strong>New</strong>: <code>createSpaOffer</code> / <code>deleteSpaOffer</code> (<code>refill-promo-calendar.functions.ts</code>), migration <code>v2_00_0_spa_authored_offers</code> (<code>source</code> column + nullable manufacturer). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>scheduling.functions.ts</code> (self-book win + service snapshot), <code>promo-calendar.ts</code> (offer id/source), <code>app.refill.recognition.rewards.tsx</code> (authoring card), <code>changelog.ts</code>.",
