      "<strong>v1.45.0 &mdash; WYSIWYG inline edit + paste/upload template seeding. The v1.44 inline-edit shipped as a raw-HTML textarea &mdash; reps saw <code>&lt;p&gt;Hi [first name],&lt;/p&gt;</code> markup, not compose-like output. Per [[feedback-human-first-design]]: computers must think like humans, not the reverse. v1.45.0 swaps that textarea for a TipTap WYSIWYG editor across all 3 surfaces (rep Outreach + rep Recruit + admin EditModal) and adds a paste-or-upload template seeder for admin.</strong> <strong>What ships</strong>: (1) NEW <code>src/components/refill/TemplateEditor.tsx</code> &mdash; TipTap-based React editor with StarterKit (bold/italic/lists/headings/blockquote), Link extension, and a custom ProseMirror Decoration plugin that renders placeholder tokens (<code>[first name]</code>, <code>$[exact figure]</code>, <code>[my commission rate]</code>, etc.) as inline chips. Underlying text stays as the bracketed literal &mdash; same shape the server <code>substitutePlaceholders</code> regex in <code>refill-outreach-send.ts</code> already consumes; no round-trip serializer needed. Toolbar: Bold, Italic, Link, Bulleted list, Numbered list, Undo. Light-bg styling, self-contained CSS, ~350 LOC. (2) Wired into <code>app.rep.outreach.tsx</code> SendPanel (replaces the per-send <code>bodyOverride</code> textarea), <code>app.rep.recruit.tsx</code> SendPanel (same), and <code>app.admin.outreach.tsx</code> EditModal (non-Loom channels &mdash; Loom scripts keep the plain Textarea since they're read aloud, not rendered). (3) NEW <code>src/components/refill/TemplateBulkImport.tsx</code> &mdash; paste-or-upload modal for seeding the template library from any source. Accepts raw paste, <code>.txt</code>, <code>.md</code>, and <code>.docx</code> (via <code>mammoth.js</code>). Auto-detects multi-message docs by splitting on <code>---</code> separators (markdown HR for text/md; <code>&lt;hr&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;p&gt;---&lt;/p&gt;</code> for HTML from mammoth). Auto-extracts subject from leading <code>Subject: …</code> line per message. Each parsed message lands in a review card with editable subject + TipTap body + ICP + channel + audience (spa/rep) selectors. Save-all calls the existing <code>bulkUpsertOutreachTemplates</code> path. Mounted alongside the existing HTML-pack import on <code>/app/admin/outreach</code> &mdash; two buttons, two mental models (HTML pack = structured Refill-Outreach-Pack.html doc; Paste/upload = any source). (4) Server fn <code>bulkUpsertOutreachTemplates</code> in <code>refill-outreach.ts</code> extended: <code>templateInputSchema</code> gains optional <code>audience</code> field; existing-active lookup scopes by audience so a new rep-audience template doesn't accidentally deactivate the matching spa-audience template with the same (icp, channel) tuple. Back-compat preserved &mdash; the HTML-pack importer doesn't pass audience and defaults to 'spa' which matches its prior behavior. <strong>Why this matters</strong>: reps are not engineers. Markdown asterisks visible in an editor = the computer leaking through. Per [[feedback-ux-standard]]: perfection is the baseline. Per [[feedback-setup-wizards-auto-advance]]: every friction point is a customer-loss risk &mdash; same applies to authoring friction on the rep tools. The paste/upload path lets admin seed templates from Notes / Word / Gmail draft / any source in seconds instead of HTML-marker-hand-coding. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T ship</strong>: rep-side template upload (would require per-rep template scoping; current <code>outreach_templates</code> is a shared library &mdash; deferred to a follow-up ship if Kelly/Karen request it); atomic-delete placeholder semantics (chips render via Decoration; rep can still backspace through a token char-by-char &mdash; v2 concern); frontdoor password-protect (queued for post-demo tomorrow per stealth-first doctrine, NOT touching creds before a demo). <strong>Dependencies added</strong>: <code>@tiptap/react</code>, <code>@tiptap/pm</code>, <code>@tiptap/starter-kit</code>, <code>@tiptap/extension-link</code>, <code>mammoth</code>. ~72 new package descendants. Bundle: admin.outreach chunk grew to 1.11MB (TipTap + mammoth) &mdash; admin-only surface, not on the critical path. <strong>Touched</strong>: 2 NEW files (<code>TemplateEditor.tsx</code>, <code>TemplateBulkImport.tsx</code>), <code>src/routes/app.rep.outreach.tsx</code> (+ editor import + replaced textarea), <code>src/routes/app.rep.recruit.tsx</code> (+ editor import + replaced textarea), <code>src/routes/app.admin.outreach.tsx</code> (+ TemplateBulkImport mount + Paste/upload button + FileText icon + audience-passthrough wired via existing bulk handler), <code>src/server/refill-outreach.ts</code> (+ audience in templateInputSchema and bulkUpsert insert), <code>src/integrations/supabase/types.ts</code> (stripped accidental Supabase CLI update-notice stomp at EOF; pre-existing, unrelated to feature), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry), <code>package.json</code> + <code>package-lock.json</code> (deps). No new migrations; no wrangler.jsonc change.",
