      "<strong>v1.43.3 &mdash; Vagaro install wizard: Rejuv-tested onboarding playbook. Per <code>project-customer-as-developer-access</code> doctrine banked this ship: Refill can&rsquo;t proxy Rejuv&rsquo;s Vagaro API key for other spas (per-merchant model), BUT we can replay Rejuv&rsquo;s proven onboarding path for every other spa &mdash; collapsing the install flow from &lsquo;figure it out + risk a denial&rsquo; to &lsquo;follow this 60-second guided playbook + 7-day wait.&rsquo;</strong> <strong>What ships</strong>: <code>src/routes/app.refill.settings.vagaro-install.tsx</code> rewritten with a 4-step guided wizard replacing the prior 2-step paste-and-go flow. <strong>Step 1 (Prerequisites)</strong>: Vagaro Pro plan (not free trial), computer/tablet/Pay Desk/PayPro version, Vagaro CC Processing active &mdash; with deep-link to <code>vagaro.com/pro/pricing</code> if signup needed. <strong>Step 2 (Submit API request)</strong>: deep-link to Vagaro&rsquo;s actual API/Webhooks Contact form &mdash; <code>form.asana.com/?k=SX3qQGg2syKV53wH-rl34w&amp;d=35883393372079</code> &mdash; the Asana-hosted form Grasshopper discovered during Rejuv onboarding 2026-06-03 (which scout extraction missed: scout described the gate structure but didn&rsquo;t extract the form URL itself). Plus a <strong>pre-written use-case template</strong> with one-tap clipboard copier: the template describes the spa&rsquo;s operational need (cancellation rebooking + waitlist outreach, ~8-12% revenue recovery) WITHOUT mentioning the Refill brand &mdash; minimizes aggregate Refill-brand signal at Vagaro&rsquo;s review queue per the stealth-posture refinement banked in <code>project-vagaro-priority-reframe</code>. Form-event checkboxes called out explicitly (Customers + Appointments + Transactions + Form Submissions). <strong>Step 3 (Wait)</strong>: sets expectations (~7 business days; Rejuv cleared in 4); explicitly states the &lsquo;minor add-on fee&rsquo; using Vagaro&rsquo;s exact wording (per Gemini transcript Grasshopper sourced) &mdash; addresses the unverified $10/mo claim by routing pricing through Vagaro Enterprise Sales rather than asserting a specific number. <strong>Step 4 (Generate key + paste)</strong>: correct path surfaced &mdash; <code>Settings &rarr; Developers &rarr; APIs &amp; Webhooks</code> (NOT the v1.38.0&rsquo;s incorrect <code>Settings &rarr; API</code>). <strong>NEW component</strong>: <code>UseCaseTemplateCopier</code> &mdash; clipboard-API + ephemeral &lsquo;Copied&rsquo; check-state for 3s + sonner toast. Per <code>feedback_copy_paste_actionables</code>: reduces friction at the Asana form to tap-once-paste-once. <strong>Why this matters strategically</strong>: every Vagaro merchant who lands on Refill&rsquo;s wizard hits a proven path Rejuv already validated. No trial-and-error. No misframed use-case field. No skipped prerequisites. Rejuv&rsquo;s real-customer status compresses the SMB onboarding flow for every subsequent Vagaro spa &mdash; the structural advantage no pure-software competitor has. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T ship</strong>: Refill-side proxy of Rejuv&rsquo;s API key (architecturally impossible &mdash; Vagaro&rsquo;s per-merchant model issues keys tied to each account); per-spa platform-subdomain capture (Vagaro is single-domain so N/A); auto-population of form fields (Asana&rsquo;s form is third-party HTML; we deep-link + clipboard-template only). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/routes/app.refill.settings.vagaro-install.tsx</code> (extensive: 2-step &rarr; 4-step + 3 new constants + UseCaseTemplateCopier component), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No schema change; no new dependencies; no wrangler.jsonc change.",
