      "<strong>v1.43.2 &mdash; Vagaro connector ground-truth from public docs scout. 3 v1.38.0 architecture-pre-build guesses corrected against verbatim Vagaro Public Developer Docs (docs.vagaro.com scout 2026-06-03). Stealth-first doctrine applied recursively: Vagaro&rsquo;s docs are FULLY PUBLIC with zero identification cost &mdash; we extracted the entire webhook envelope shape + 11-value bookingStatus enum + appointment payload field names without paying for a merchant account.</strong> <strong>Bug 1 &mdash; Webhook envelope shape</strong>: v1.38.0 expected <code>{ event, eventId/id, merchantId/businessId, occurredAt/createdAt, data }</code> based on architecture-pre-build best-guess. Reality (verbatim from docs.vagaro.com): <code>{ id, createdDate, type, action, payload }</code> where <code>type</code> is the bucket (appointment / customer / formResponse / transaction / business_location / employee) and <code>action</code> is the verb (created / updated / deleted). parseVagaroWebhookBody now combines <code>type + action</code> into the v1.38.0-style &lsquo;type.action&rsquo; event string with backward-compat fallback to legacy <code>event</code> field if present. <code>createdDate</code> replaces <code>occurredAt</code>/<code>createdAt</code>. <code>payload</code> replaces <code>data</code>. Connector accepts both new and legacy field names for forward + backward compatibility. <strong>Bug 2 &mdash; bookingStatus enum mismatch</strong>: v1.38.0 had 6 camelCase guesses (Booked / Confirmed / CheckedIn / Completed / Cancelled / NoShow). Reality is 11 verbatim values with spaces and human-readable form: Accepted / Awaiting Confirmation / Cancel / Confirmed / Deleted / Denied / Need Acceptance / No Show / Ready to Start / Service Completed / Service In Progress / Show. Status enum union expanded to include all 17 (11 verbatim + 6 legacy aliases). vagaroStatusToRefillStatus mapper rewritten to handle all 17 with intent-aware grouping: cancellation family (Cancel / Deleted / Denied + legacy Cancelled), no-show family (No Show + legacy NoShow), terminal-happy (Service Completed / Show + legacy Completed / CheckedIn), active forward-looking (Accepted / Awaiting Confirmation / Confirmed / Need Acceptance / Ready to Start / Service In Progress + legacy Booked). <strong>Bug 3 &mdash; appointment payload field names</strong>: docs surface <code>appointmentId / bookingStatus / startTime / endTime / customerId / serviceProviderId / businessId / amount / eventType / onlineVsInhouse / appointmentTypeCode / appointmentTypeName / bookingSource / calendarEventId / formResponseIds[]</code>. v1.38.0 used REST-style guesses (<code>id / status / startDateTime / staffId / serviceId / notes</code>) which may have been right for REST API responses but wrong for webhook payloads. VagaroAppointmentRaw type expanded to cover BOTH variants; rawToAppointment uses tolerant fallback chain (appointmentId &rArr; id, bookingStatus &rArr; status, startTime &rArr; startDateTime, serviceProviderId &rArr; staffId, etc.). Falls back gracefully if either form is missing. <strong>Bug 0 (signature scheme) &mdash; ALREADY CORRECT</strong>: v1.38.0 verifyVagaroWebhookSignature already used shared-token constant-time equality (NOT HMAC). Scout confirmed this is the right scheme. No change needed; v1.35.x doctrine timing-attack-defense pattern stands. <strong>Strategic implications surfaced by this scout</strong>: (1) Vagaro is the LARGEST TAM of the 6 platforms scouted today (220K+ professionals, 95%+ at 1-10 employees) and has the WORST native recovery tooling (Waitlist is notify-only, not recovery-revenue-engine) &mdash; arguably Refill&rsquo;s #1 outreach target, not the &lsquo;defer to candidate pool&rsquo; framing v1.38.0 banked. (2) The $10/mo API fee in our memory was likely conflated with Vagaro&rsquo;s $10/mo Large-Merchant CC-processing surcharge; actual API fee structure routes through Enterprise Sales and isn&rsquo;t public &mdash; treat as unverified pending first merchant. (3) docs.vagaro.com is fully public; Refill identification risk is ZERO. Scout report banked at Refill-Gated-Vendor-Stealth-Map-v1.html. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T ship</strong>: REST API field-name validation (we only ground-truthed the webhook payload; the REST appointment shape may differ &mdash; defer to first real merchant onboarding). The 6 outbound IP whitelist (Vagaro publishes these only post-activation in merchant portal). Actual rate-limit ceilings (zero public docs; first real merchant will surface). project_multi_scheduler_thesis memory update (Vagaro priority elevation from &lsquo;defer&rsquo; to &lsquo;#1 outreach&rsquo;) &mdash; separate housekeeping. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/lib/schedulers/vagaro.ts</code> (VagaroAppointmentStatus type expanded; vagaroStatusToRefillStatus rewritten; VagaroAppointmentRaw type expanded; rawToAppointment field-name fallback chain; parseVagaroWebhookBody envelope shape corrected), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No schema change; no new files; no new dependencies.",
