      "<strong>v1.43.1 &mdash; Mindbody comprehensive sandbox intel sweep route. Strategic pivot: Grasshopper&rsquo;s CTO-grade call 2026-06-03 &mdash; stay in stealth/sandbox mode with Mindbody until we&rsquo;ve fully exhausted the platform surface, so even a Go-Live DENIAL leaves us with complete competitive intel. Boulevard&rsquo;s denial (Jira DS-4790) taught the asymmetric-risk lesson: requesting Go Live identifies Refill to the vendor + lets them study us + gives them a chance to say no. The sandbox is anonymous-ish + extractive. Banked as feedback_stealth_first_doctrine memory + applies across all gated vendors (Mindbody, Booker, Jane, Zenoti &mdash; Mangomint excepted, no public surface).</strong> <strong>What lands</strong>: NEW <code>src/routes/api.integrations.mindbody.sandbox-intel-sweep.ts</code> (~245 LOC) &mdash; read-only comprehensive probe across 13 Mindbody Public API v6 endpoints + Webhooks API. Auth chain reuses the confirmed sandbox login (mindbodysandboxsite@gmail.com / Apitest1234 per v1.42.2 4-candidate probe). For each endpoint: hits with Api-Key + SiteId=-99 + Bearer header, captures status / ok / top keys / pagination shape / per-array { count, firstItemKeys, firstItemSample }. Surfaces failed endpoints + error bodies for diagnostic. <strong>Probed surface</strong>: <code>/site/sites</code> (already covered) + <code>/site/locations</code> (multi-location support) + <code>/site/sessiontypes</code> (services taxonomy &mdash; CRITICAL for treatment_type mapping) + <code>/site/programs</code> + <code>/class/classdescriptions</code> + <code>/staff/staff</code> (sampled) + <code>/client/clients</code> (sampled) + <code>/appointment/bookableitems</code> (booking-write shape probe) + <code>/sale/sales</code> + <code>/sale/services</code> + <code>/sale/packages</code> + <code>/subscriptions/eventIds</code> (LIST of all webhook event types available) + <code>/subscriptions/subscriptions</code> (LIST current webhook subscriptions on the partner key). <strong>Read-only by design</strong>: no POSTs / PUTs / DELETEs in this sweep. Sandbox writes wipe nightly but we stay invisible to whoever monitors -99 traffic by sticking to GETs. <strong>Roll-up summary</strong>: counts of working endpoints + list of failed labels for triage. <strong>Strategic anchor</strong>: per <code>feedback_stealth_first_doctrine</code> banked this ship + <code>user_dog_years_thesis</code> + <code>project_platforms_pre_built_architecture</code>: every day of stealth extraction = a day of velocity compounded into the substrate while Refill remains invisible to Mindbody. If Mindbody ever denies our Go-Live (whenever we finally submit), we still have: full endpoint catalog, response shapes, webhook event types, payload shapes, integration substrate &mdash; AKA: Lite Mode parser fully tuned + per-platform sales sheet of what we DO support + comprehensive sandbox demo &mdash; and the only thing we lose is production webhook real-time signal which Lite Mode already covers ~70% of for free. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T ship</strong>: actual write tests (POST appointment / addclient / createSubscription) &mdash; deferred until we&rsquo;ve absorbed everything from reads + decided which writes we need to verify before Go-Live ever happens. Webhook subscription CREATE in sandbox (could expose Refill&rsquo;s URL pattern to Mindbody&rsquo;s aggregated logs &mdash; defer). <strong>Touched</strong>: 1 NEW route, <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No schema change; no new dependencies; reuses existing sandbox secrets in CF (MINDBODY_SANDBOX_API_KEY).",
