      "<strong>v1.43.0 &mdash; Lite Mode Recovery loop closed end-to-end. Deep-link writeback flow ships per Refill-LightMode-Spec-v1.html &sect;4 + Refill-Followups-Plan-v1.html P2-1. When a rescue claim lands on a Lite Mode connection (emma_appointments.source matches /^lite-/), Refill composes + sends the spa owner an email with a deeplink to the relevant vendor portal + a copy-paste payload of patient + slot details. Owner taps deeplink &rarr; portal opens &rarr; books rescued-in patient manually in &lt;30 seconds. The vendor&rsquo;s own confirmation email triggered by that manual book parses through the existing Lite Mode pipeline + closes the loop automatically.</strong> <strong>This is the moat moment</strong>: Lite Mode without writeback was a half-product (one-way signal feed). With writeback, Refill&rsquo;s full Recovery loop works on platforms we have ZERO API access to. The sales demo collapses from a staged hand-wave to a single coherent narrative: 60-second Gmail-filter setup &rarr; real cancellation arrives &rarr; Refill matches + texts patient &rarr; patient taps yes &rarr; owner gets one-tap-confirm email &rarr; book lands in portal &rarr; next email parse closes the loop. <strong>What lands in this ship</strong>: (1) NEW <code>src/lib/light-mode/writeback.ts</code> (~135 LOC) &mdash; pure builders (no Supabase coupling): <code>buildClaimDeeplink(args)</code> returns per-platform { url, supportsPrefill, cta, instructions } with verified deeplink patterns where publicly known (Mindbody clients.mindbodyonline.com/classic/ws?studioid=&lt;siteId&gt;, Boulevard dashboard.joinblvd.com, Booker app.booker.com, Zenoti login.zenoti.com, Jane &lt;clinic&gt;.jane.app/admin OR jane.app/login fallback). <code>buildCopyPayload(args)</code> composes the plain-text quick-copy block with patient name / phone / email / service / time / notes, one field per line per <code>feedback_copy_paste_actionables</code>. Per <code>feedback_verify_third_party_ui</code>: only confirmed paths; no guessed prefill URLs; <code>supportsPrefill: false</code> on all platforms in v1 (future polish per-platform scout). (2) NEW <code>src/server/light-mode-writeback.functions.ts</code> (~265 LOC) &mdash; <code>dispatchLightModeWriteback({ userId, appointmentId, patientNodeId, source, originalExternalId, scheduledAt })</code>. Validates source is Lite Mode (looksLikeLightModeSource discriminator), loads owner email (tenant primary_contact_email &rarr; auth.users.email fallback), loads patient attrs (first_name / last_name / phone / email) from knowledge_nodes, loads appointment treatment_type + provider_name, resolves spa platform slug from emma_scheduler_connections if a parallel API connection exists, builds deeplink + copy payload, composes plain-text + HTML email (KAREN_FROM brand consistent with refill-drip), sends via Resend /emails with tags=[type=light-mode-writeback, platform=&lt;p&gt;]. Email subject &lsquo;\u{1F389} Rescue claimed &mdash; book &lt;Patient&gt; into &lt;slot time&gt;&rsquo; (party-popper emoji per <code>feedback_keep_it_fun</code>). HTML body uses light-bg inline-CSS card layout with emerald CTA button + monospace copy-payload block. Per <code>feedback_workers_no_fire_and_forget</code>: full await chain; Resend fetch is bounded by AbortSignal.timeout(20s). (3) MODIFIED <code>src/server/emma-rescue.functions.ts</code> <code>claimRescueSlot</code> &mdash; new Lite Mode branch lands BEFORE the existing source-name discriminator. When <code>source.startsWith(&lsquo;lite-&rsquo;)</code>: dynamic import of <code>dispatchLightModeWriteback</code> + invoke with offer/claimedApt context; stamp result.notes on emma_rescue_attempts (same fail-open pattern as the existing API writeback branches). Existing 8 API-source branches (acuity / square / boulevard / mindbody / vagaro / booker / zenoti / jane) UNCHANGED. (4) <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> &mdash; this entry. <strong>Strategic anchors</strong>: per <code>project_imessage_mcp_killer_arch</code> &mdash; iMessage MCP is the patient-side primitive; owner-self notification uses plain email (lower friction, no MCP setup-step on owner&rsquo;s side). Per <code>project_platforms_pre_built_architecture</code> &mdash; same doctrine applied recursively: the deeplink substrate ships universal across all 5 platforms now; per-platform prefill-URL refinements happen as we surface them via pilot tenants. Per <code>user_dog_years_thesis</code> &mdash; one engineering session (~30 min) unlocks Recovery loop on 5 platforms simultaneously, no vendor approval needed. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T ship</strong>: per-spa Zenoti / Jane subdomain capture at Lite Mode wizard time (deeplink falls back to generic landing pages on those two; future polish ship); query-param-prefill URLs (need per-platform scout of actual portal URL formats); SMS-to-owner option (email is the v1 channel); owner-side iMessage MCP variant (deferred until a spa specifically asks). <strong>Touched</strong>: 2 NEW files (<code>src/lib/light-mode/writeback.ts</code>, <code>src/server/light-mode-writeback.functions.ts</code>), 1 EXTENDED file (<code>src/server/emma-rescue.functions.ts</code> &mdash; light-mode branch in claimRescueSlot), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No schema change; no new dependencies; no wrangler.jsonc change.",
