      "<strong>v1.42.4 &mdash; Mindbody sandbox-verify smoke walks all staff in batches to surface real Appointment object shape. Closes the &lsquo;what doesn&rsquo;t ship&rsquo; gap from v1.42.3: connector Raw field-name verification (Id vs AppointmentId, Status enum strings, NoShow bool, ClientId, SessionTypeId, StaffId, StartDateTime fields). The v1.35.x-debug-arc loop continues &mdash; sandbox iteration finds gaps, fix lands, re-verify.</strong> <strong>What changed</strong>: <code>src/routes/api.integrations.mindbody.sandbox-verify.ts</code> Step 4 replaced with a staff-walk pattern. Pulls all StaffMember IDs from Step 3&rsquo;s <code>/staff/staff</code> response (100 of 141 staff returned on first page), batches them in groups of 20, calls <code>/appointment/staffappointments</code> per batch with widened <strong>1-year-back-to-1-year-forward window</strong> (vs prior 30d-back/90d-forward) to catch any test bookings in sandbox -99 regardless of when they were created. Stops on first batch returning non-empty Appointments[]; dumps the first 2 appointment objects verbatim + lists their full key set + reports the PaginationResponse for that batch. <strong>What this surfaces</strong>: when smoke finds appointments, we know the actual Raw field names Mindbody uses; if no batch returns appointments after walking all 141 staff with the 2-year window, we know sandbox -99 truly has no appointments seeded (write a sandbox booking to seed, then re-run; or wait for production Karen-Rejuv data). Either outcome is useful debug-arc signal. <strong>Per-batch reporting</strong>: each batch summary contains batchIndex, staffIdsRange (first..last), staffIdsCount, status, ok, apptCount, totalResults &mdash; even empty batches yield diagnostic data so we can see exactly where in the staff list (if anywhere) appointments lived. <strong>Connector code unchanged</strong>: v1.42.3 fixes already shipped (listMindbodyAppointments + getMindbodyAppointment + listMindbodyStaff). This smoke ship is pure diagnostic &mdash; we&rsquo;re hitting the endpoint directly via fetch + walking staff to find data, then comparing shape against rawToAppointment&rsquo;s field-name assumptions. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/routes/api.integrations.mindbody.sandbox-verify.ts</code> (Step 4 replaced &mdash; removed 4-endpoint candidate probe since staffappointments was definitively right; added staff-walk loop with per-batch metrics + raw-shape dump on first hit), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No schema change; no new files; no new dependencies. <strong>Strategic anchor</strong>: per <code>feedback-validate-against-real-exports</code> + v1.35.x-debug-arc-doctrine, &lsquo;synthetic guesses are NOT validation; only real provider responses are.&rsquo; This walk either confirms the connector&rsquo;s rawToAppointment assumptions OR surfaces the corrections needed before Karen-Rejuv production data lands. Cheap to run (140 staff / 20 batch = 7 calls max; each call < 500ms); high information density.",
