      "<strong>v1.35.8 &mdash; Square backfill failure degraded to non-fatal (seller-onboarding state, not a credential failure). Real progress milestone: v1.35.7&rsquo;s form-encoded body fix + Grasshopper&rsquo;s sandbox-Application-Secret re-paste (the value buried on Square&rsquo;s OAuth tab, not the personal access token on the Credentials tab) finally cleared the token exchange + merchant fetch + connection upsert + webhook-degrade chain end-to-end. The connection row materialized. NEW error surfaced from a deeper step: <code>backfillSquareBookings</code> hit <code>/v2/bookings</code> and Square returned <code>401 AUTHENTICATION_ERROR UNAUTHORIZED &quot;not onboarded to Appointments&quot;</code>. That&rsquo;s a seller-config state &mdash; the Default Test Account in Grasshopper&rsquo;s sandbox doesn&rsquo;t have Square Appointments enabled &mdash; not a credentials problem. The connection itself works (token exchange is fine); there&rsquo;s just nothing for backfill to read until the seller turns on the Appointments product on their sandbox dashboard.</strong> <strong>Fix</strong>: same fail-degraded pattern v1.35.6 applied to webhook subscribe now applies to backfill. <code>backfillSquareBookings</code> failure no longer returns <code>errReturn(&quot;backfill&quot;)</code> &mdash; instead the warning gets stamped to <code>last_error</code> with a clear message (&ldquo;Square Appointments not enabled on this seller. Enable it on your Square dashboard, then hit Re-sync.&rdquo; for the specific onboarding case; generic &ldquo;Initial backfill failed (...). Hit Re-sync to retry.&rdquo; otherwise) and the connection still lands <code>status=connected</code>. <strong>Warning priority order</strong>: <code>tier_gate</code> &gt; <code>backfillWarning</code> &gt; <code>webhookWarning</code> &gt; <code>null</code>. Tier wins because it blocks writeback (the actual value-prop call); backfill + webhook warnings are read-side degradations the user can fix on their Square dashboard then re-sync. <strong>Debug arc retrospective &mdash; full chain</strong>: v1.35.0 (webhook scope gap) → v1.35.1 (added scopes) → v1.35.2 (defensive trim SQUARE_ENV value) → v1.35.3 (SQUARE_ENV into wrangler.jsonc, deploys were wiping the dashboard-side var) → v1.35.4 (whitespace strip credentials + bubble Square error to URL + length logging) → v1.35.5 (redirect_uri in token body) → v1.35.6 (drop partner-tier webhook scopes; degrade webhook subscribe to non-fatal) → v1.35.7 (form-encoded body per OAuth 2.0 RFC) → Grasshopper re-pasted the Sandbox Application Secret from the OAuth tab (NOT the Access token from the Credentials tab &mdash; Square&rsquo;s UI has two confusingly-similar pages and the OAuth-required secret only lives on one) → v1.35.8 (degrade backfill non-fatal because some sandbox sellers aren&rsquo;t onboarded to Appointments). The v1.35.4 logging ship was the unlock for everything that followed &mdash; without surfacing Square&rsquo;s actual error text + credential lengths, we&rsquo;d still be guessing. <strong>Architectural learning banked across the arc</strong>: (1) any OAuth callback that catches errors MUST bubble actual provider error text to the user-visible redirect URL or settings dashboard (v1.35.4 pattern), (2) credential value length logging surfaces type-confusion (access-token vs application-secret) before code-fix iterations begin, (3) every callback step that touches an external provider needs explicit fail-degrade-vs-fail-fast semantics declared at design time (steps that block the connection&rsquo;s value-prop fail fast; steps that block fringe read-sync degrade), (4) Cloudflare dashboard plaintext vars + observability config are EPHEMERAL relative to wrangler deploys; anything that must survive deploys lives in wrangler.jsonc, (5) Cloudflare secret input fields can leak whitespace into stored values; defensive strip + length-log pattern is the workaround. Same patterns now need to land on Mindbody, Boulevard, JaneApp OAuth handlers when they ship. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/routes/api.integrations.square.oauth-callback.ts</code> (backfill try/catch now stamps warning instead of errReturn; warning priority added to status=&quot;connected&quot; lastError chain), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No schema change; no new dependencies; no Worker secret changes.",
