      "<strong>v1.35.3 &mdash; SQUARE_ENV migrated to wrangler.jsonc. The actual root cause of the production-routing bug surfaced under v1.35.2 diagnosis: SQUARE_ENV was added manually as a Cloudflare-dashboard plaintext var when v1.35.0 first shipped, but every subsequent <code>npm run deploy</code> wiped it because wrangler enforces the <code>vars</code> block from <code>wrangler.jsonc</code> as the authoritative plaintext-var list &mdash; anything in the dashboard but not the config file gets stripped.</strong> v1.35.1 deploy and v1.35.2 deploy each wiped SQUARE_ENV. At runtime <code>process.env.SQUARE_ENV</code> returned <code>undefined</code>, the strict-equality check defaulted to the production branch, and the OAuth URL routed against <code>app.squareup.com</code> using SQUARE_APP_ID (production credentials) against Grasshopper&rsquo;s real Rejuv Skin Spa production Square account &mdash; not the sandbox test account. v1.35.2&rsquo;s whitespace-contamination hypothesis was wrong; the var was simply missing entirely each time. <strong>Real fix</strong>: added <code>&quot;SQUARE_ENV&quot;: &quot;sandbox&quot;</code> to the <code>vars</code> block in <code>wrangler.jsonc</code>. Now wrangler deploys push SQUARE_ENV from config every time + it never disappears. <strong>v1.35.2&rsquo;s <code>resolveSquareEnv()</code> hardening still stands</strong> &mdash; defensive trim + lowercase remains the right pattern for ANY runtime config string-equality check, and now-tested catches both whitespace contamination AND case variation should either ever surface in the future. <strong>Architectural learning banked</strong>: Cloudflare Worker plaintext vars added via dashboard UI are EPHEMERAL relative to wrangler deploys. Only secrets (set via <code>wrangler secret put</code>) persist across deploys. Any plaintext config that needs to survive deploys MUST live in <code>wrangler.jsonc</code>. This pattern needs to land on every future scheduler env-var (MINDBODY_ENV, BOULEVARD_ENV, etc.) and every cron-trigger config var. The deploy-bindings printout (visible in <code>npm run deploy</code> tail) lists only vars from wrangler.jsonc &mdash; a fast sanity-check that a new plaintext var has been added to config-side, not dashboard-side. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>wrangler.jsonc</code> (1 line added to vars), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No code change; no migration; no Worker secret change. <strong>Companion cleanup owed (manual)</strong>: the v1.35.0 first OAuth attempt established a production-side grant on Grasshopper&rsquo;s real Rejuv Square account (visible at <code>app.squareup.com/dashboard/apps/my-applications</code> as &lsquo;Refill &middot; Connected 18 minutes ago&rsquo;). That grant persists on Square&rsquo;s server even after Refill&rsquo;s local Disconnect &mdash; Grasshopper needs to click Disconnect App on Square&rsquo;s production dashboard to fully revoke it.",
