      "<strong>v1.34.5 &mdash; Recognition Allocation Engine. The 4th Refill agent, the moat ship of the v1.34 arc.</strong> Per <code>project_recognition_allocation_engine_spec</code>: Recognition mechanics select silently → patients discover they were chosen → spas reinforce existing good behavior. Architecturally incumbent-uncatchable because the delivery primitive (Karen-Mac iMessage) requires owner-identity messaging that Vagaro/Mindbody/Boulevard structurally can&rsquo;t do. <strong>What ships</strong>: the engine that scores patients into three cohorts (Loyal Vintage / Top-Decile Current / At-Risk Overlay), splits available rebate inventory across them per Karen&rsquo;s 40/40/20 default (Karen-adjustable per period), and queues allocation suggestions Karen confirms one-by-one. <strong>New server fn module</strong> <code>src/server/refill-recognition-allocation.functions.ts</code> (~450 lines): <code>getAllocationSettings</code> / <code>updateAllocationSettings</code> (cohort splits + cooldown + manual-confirm gate, persisted via knowledge_nodes pattern); <code>listAllocationSuggestions</code> (with status pending / confirmed / dismissed); <code>confirmAllocationSuggestion</code> (decrements rebate_inventory_units.units_deployed on confirm); <code>dismissAllocationSuggestion</code>; <code>runAllocation</code> (the engine itself). <strong>Engine flow</strong> (runAllocation): (1) load available rebate_inventory_units (units_total − units_deployed > 0) + join brand/manufacturer metadata from knowledge_nodes. (2) Load all patient knowledge_nodes (5000-row cap; tenant-scoped). (3) Compute spend-decile cutoff (90th percentile of netSpendUsd > 0). (4) Score every patient → classify into ONE cohort: At-Risk if lastVisit 60-180d ago AND spend > 0; Top-Decile Current if netSpend ≥ cutoff AND lastVisit < 180d; Loyal Vintage if first-visit > 365d ago AND lastVisit < 180d AND totalVisits ≥ 4; else excluded. (5) Drop patients with a confirmed suggestion within cooldown window (12mo default). (6) Split total available units 40/40/20 (or per Karen&rsquo;s split) into per-cohort targets. (7) Per cohort, take top-N by score, greedy-allocate one unit per patient from the brand with most remaining inventory. (8) Persist as knowledge_nodes rows (node_type=&lsquo;allocation_suggestion&rsquo;, attachments hold the full suggestion shape including patient + cohort + brand + manufacturer + units + score + rationale + status). <strong>Operator UI</strong> at <code>/app/refill/agents/recognition</code>: PageHeader with &lsquo;Run allocation&rsquo; CTA + AgentsTabStrip (now 4 tabs: Preshow / Rescue / Attribution / Recognition). &lsquo;Recognition, not discounts&rsquo; explainer banner (frames the engine&rsquo;s philosophy; links to Inventory + Manufacturers). Pending-allocations overview card with 3-cohort grid (count + cohort description). Cohort split + cooldown editor (4 number inputs with Save button + sum-to-100 client-side validation). Allocation queue list (latest 100, with per-row patient link + cohort chip + brand+manufacturer pill + score + rationale + Confirm/Dismiss buttons; row-state changes inline after action). v1.34.5 disclaimer card flagging delivery integration lands in v1.34.x. <strong>AgentsTabStrip</strong> extended to 4 tabs with Award icon for Recognition; existing Preshow/Rescue/Attribution pages render the strip in the same place so cross-nav remains clean. <strong>Recognition Inventory + Manufacturers</strong>: still accessible via the dedicated Recognition nav chip (substrate); the Agent surface (engine) is reached via the Agents nav chip + Recognition tab. Two different mental models, two different starting points &mdash; Karen lands wherever matches her intent. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T ship (queued)</strong>: ACTUAL iMessage delivery via Karen-Mac MCP bridge (v1.34.x next &mdash; until then Confirm = &ldquo;I&rsquo;ll reach out personally&rdquo;); nightly cron that auto-runs allocation (Karen taps Run allocation manually for now); message templating per cohort (each suggestion has a rationale string Karen reads, no auto-composed SMS yet); per-brand affinity inference (manual brand list from Manufacturer profile flows through); outcome tracking + cross-spa benchmarking (spec §5/§6, future ship); sparkline + before/after performance chart (needs 30d+ of post-Allocation-era data); milestone-aware cooldown overrides (10yr anniversary, post-recovery, birthday — currently 12mo flat); per-treatment cooldown granularity. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/server/refill-recognition-allocation.functions.ts</code> (new, ~450 lines), <code>src/routes/app.refill.agents.recognition.tsx</code> (new, ~470 lines), <code>src/components/refill/AgentsTabStrip.tsx</code> (Award icon import + Recognition tab), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no schema; no new dependencies. Builds entirely on substrate primitives from v1.34.2 (rebate_inventory_units), v1.34.2.2 (manufacturer_profile), and the knowledge_nodes patient summary primitive that&rsquo;s existed since v341 patient architecture. <strong>Strategic anchor</strong>: per [[project-recognition-allocation-engine-spec]] this is the engine. Allergan-spend → higher Alle for Business rebate tier → larger inventory next quarter → more patients recognized → recognized patients continue buying Allergan → spa Allergan-spend ↑. Same compounding incumbents have, pointed at retention instead of acquisition. v1.34.x closes the delivery loop.",
