      "<strong>v1.34.2.1 &mdash; Hotfix: PersonaSwitcher revert-to-admin didn&rsquo;t smart-route. Admin switching from Kelly (Rep) or Karen (Spa Owner) back to Admin while on <code>/app/rep</code> or <code>/app/refill</code> stayed on that URL instead of landing in the admin shell &mdash; producing either the &ldquo;Your account isn&rsquo;t set up as a Refill rep yet&rdquo; empty state (RepShell with no rep_accounts row) or the &ldquo;Defaulted to Rejuv Skin Spa&rdquo; banner (RefillShell admin fallback to first-tenant). Grasshopper hit this 2026-06-02 morning walking the persona-switcher flow.</strong> <strong>Root cause</strong>: v1.24.3 generalized smart-routing (<code>pickRedirectForPersonaSwitch</code> in <code>src/lib/admin-view-as.ts</code>) covered the non-admin selection branch but explicitly NOT the revert-to-admin branch. The docstring even called it out: &ldquo;Reverting to admin (caller&rsquo;s own shell) → undefined → stay.&rdquo; The PersonaSwitcher&rsquo;s onChange used <code>setAdminViewAsUserId(null)</code> without computing a redirect target. The intent was &ldquo;stay where you were so admin can keep poking at the surface they were just viewing.&rdquo; In practice, admin has no rep_account and no spa-owner tenant_membership of their own &mdash; the rep + spa-owner shells fall through to empty states, not a coherent admin view. <strong>The fix</strong>: PersonaSwitcher.onChange revert branch now calls <code>pickRedirectForPersonaSwitch(window.location.pathname, &quot;admin&quot;)</code> exactly the same way the non-admin selection branch already does. The function logic ALREADY returned &ldquo;/app&rdquo; when URL shell-kind &ne; admin (the predicate was <code>urlKind !== target</code> with target=admin) &mdash; only the caller needed to invoke it. Three behaviors result, all correct: (a) admin reverts from <code>/app/admin/*</code> → urlKind=admin, target=admin, function returns undefined → setAdminViewAsUserId(null) reloads in place → admin lands back on the same admin tool they were viewing. (b) admin reverts from <code>/app/refill</code> or <code>/app/billing</code> → urlKind=spa-owner ≠ admin → function returns &ldquo;/app&rdquo; → setAdminViewAsUserId(null, &quot;/app&quot;) → /app auto-dispatches to admin shell home (/app/admin). (c) admin reverts from <code>/app/rep</code> → urlKind=rep ≠ admin → same &ldquo;/app&rdquo; redirect → admin shell home. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: the v1.24.4-era three-personas allowlist gate is unchanged (PersonaSwitcher still filters to caller + DEMO_PERSONA_EMAILS + ADMIN_VIEWABLE_REAL_EMAILS). The &lsquo;Defaulted to&hellip;&rsquo; v1.26.20 amber banner still shows correctly when admin lands on /app/refill via auto-dispatch without an explicit pick &mdash; that&rsquo;s a separate but adjacent path. The fix here is strictly the explicit-pick-revert flow. <strong>Architectural note</strong>: docstring on <code>pickRedirectForPersonaSwitch</code> updated &mdash; the old &ldquo;Reverting to admin → undefined → stay&rdquo; bullet was misleading (true only when admin is already on an admin URL). Now reads correctly. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/components/admin/PersonaSwitcher.tsx</code> (revert branch computes redirectTo via pickRedirectForPersonaSwitch with target=&lsquo;admin&rsquo;), <code>src/lib/admin-view-as.ts</code> (docstring corrected to match actual behavior), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no schema; no new deps. Tiny diff, big quality-of-life fix on the persona-switching flow Grasshopper uses every walk-through.",
