      "<strong>v1.34.2 &mdash; Recognition Allocation Engine: Pool Entry substrate. First surface of the strategic moat ship the engine no incumbent can structurally match.</strong> Per the 2026-06-02 scout of the manufacturer-rebate substrate (Galderma / Evolus / Allergan portal exports vs off-the-record sample-bridge dynamics) and Grasshopper&rsquo;s &ldquo;THIS IS THE NITTY GRITTY OF THE BUSINESS THAT THE MONO PLATFORMS DON&rsquo;T/CAN&rsquo;T COMPREHEND&rdquo; framing, this ship lays down the inventory substrate that v1.34.3 will score + allocate against and v1.34.4 will deliver via iMessage MCP. <strong>Documentation wall held at schema level</strong>: two distinct knowledge_node types ensure that the off-the-record portion of rebate sourcing can NEVER be reverse-engineered from the database, even by accident. (1) <code>rebate_inventory_documented</code> holds portal-issued credits (Alle for Business / Allergan APP / Galderma Aspire / Evolus official promos) with provenance fields in attachments &mdash; manufacturer, programName, programPeriod, sourceRef, earnedDate, expiresDate. (2) <code>rebate_inventory_anonymous</code> holds on-hand product with NO provenance fields at all (not nullable &mdash; absent). Two separate node_types instead of one with nullable source columns so a missing-field inference can&rsquo;t recover the off-the-record signal. No <code>reps</code> table, no <code>deals</code> table, no per-row link to a specific verbal negotiation &mdash; the deal context lives entirely in Karen&rsquo;s head per the scout-locked wall. <strong>Unit lifecycle in dedicated table</strong>: <code>rebate_inventory_units</code> (one row per inventory node, 1:1 unique on node_id) tracks units_total / units_deployed with atomic UPDATE semantics. Allocation increments (in v1.34.3) get correct concurrency-safe semantics; the lifecycle stays queryable without parsing JSONB. Constraint enforced at the DB layer: <code>units_deployed &lt;= units_total</code> &mdash; the application + the schema both refuse over-allocation. Soft delete via <code>soft_deleted_at</code> preserves audit trail. Two partial indexes: hot-path (active inventory by user_id) and allocation-engine (rows with deployable units remaining). <strong>Server fns at <code>src/server/refill-recognition.functions.ts</code></strong>: 5 createServerFn handlers &mdash; <code>listRebateInventory</code> (joins knowledge_nodes + rebate_inventory_units, returns unified RebateInventoryEntry shape with kind discriminator), <code>createDocumentedInventory</code> + <code>createAnonymousInventory</code> (mint node + lifecycle row atomically, with rollback on units-insert failure since the SDK has no tx), <code>updateRebateInventory</code> (refuses units_total below already-deployed), <code>deleteRebateInventory</code> (soft delete only). Auth pattern matches refill-catalog.ts verbatim: verifyAuth &rarr; resolveEffectiveUserId (admin viewAs honored). Zod validation including regex for ISO date fields and integer bounds on unit counts. <strong>UI surface at <code>/app/refill/recognition/inventory</code></strong>: PageHeader + two Add buttons (Portal-issued / On-hand) + groups of inline-editable cards. Click any row to expand the edit form; Delete inside the edit form. Documented entries render with program-name pill + earned/expires dates + manufacturer-relevant detail; anonymous entries render minimal (brand + SKU + units + notes). Available-units count at the top of the page aggregates across all entries. Empty state with guided CTA. Mobile-responsive (Karen on phone is the design target). <strong>Nav chip + dashboard card</strong>: Recognition added to RefillNav between Promos and Recovery (8 chips total now in the &lsquo;data primitives + actions&rsquo; cluster) and to the RefillHome dashboard quick-actions grid (8 cards in the lg:grid-cols-4 layout, balanced 4+4). Award icon for the chip + card. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T ship (queued for follow-ons)</strong>: Manufacturer Profile snapshot surface at <code>/app/refill/recognition/profile</code> with tier-status from portal pastes (v1.34.2.1). AI extraction via Claude Sonnet 4.6 to parse portal screenshots into structured inventory entries (v1.34.2.1). Cohort scoring engine for the three-cohort split (Loyal Vintage 40% / Top-Decile Current 40% / At-Risk 20%) &mdash; reuses resolveCohort from emma-campaigns.functions.ts (v1.34.3). Allocation engine that intersects available inventory with patient primaryManufacturer + scoring (v1.34.3). Review + override UI + iMessage MCP delivery via Karen-Mac (v1.34.4). <strong>Migration</strong>: <code>supabase/migrations/20260622000000_v1_34_2_rebate_inventory_units.sql</code> &mdash; one new table, two RLS policies (user-owned + service-role), two partial indexes, defensive constraints. Pasted into Supabase dashboard per [[feedback-migrations-via-dashboard]]. <strong>Strategic anchor</strong>: per <code>project_recognition_allocation_engine_spec</code> v0.1 the Recognition Engine is incumbent-uncatchable because (1) the iMessage MCP delivery path (Karen-Mac) routes through Karen&rsquo;s Apple ID not a platform shortcode, and (2) the off-the-record sample-bridge dynamic is structurally unmodelable by Vagaro / Mindbody / Square / Zenoti / Boulevard because they&rsquo;d expose themselves to manufacturer ad-partner compliance. Refill builds for the operator&rsquo;s reality, behind the spa-tenant data wall. v1.34.2 is the substrate every downstream Recognition ship reads from. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>supabase/migrations/20260622000000_v1_34_2_rebate_inventory_units.sql</code> (new file, 1 new table, RLS, indexes), <code>src/server/refill-recognition.functions.ts</code> (new file, ~470 lines, 5 server fns), <code>src/routes/app.refill.recognition.inventory.tsx</code> (new file, ~640 lines, Pool Entry surface), <code>src/components/refill/RefillNav.tsx</code> (Recognition chip + RefillNavKey union extended), <code>src/components/refill/RefillShellChrome.tsx</code> (deriveActiveKey adds /app/refill/recognition &rarr; &lsquo;recognition&rsquo;), <code>src/components/refill/RefillHome.tsx</code> (Recognition action card + Award icon import), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). One new dep: none. New tables: 1. New nav chip: 1. New routes: 1.",
