      "<strong>v1.34.1.1 &mdash; Hotfix: PersonaSwitcher allowlist out of sync with the v1.28.0 Karen auth-email rename. Karen&rsquo;s real production tenant was invisible in the admin dropdown for the past 2 days because the canonical allowlist was checking against a now-defunct email.</strong> Surfaced during the v1.34.1 coherency-pass walk-through when Grasshopper switched PersonaSwitcher to &lsquo;Rejuv Skin Spa&rsquo; expecting to see 1,140 patients + 217 catalog rows, got 1 patient + 0 catalog instead. Two-step diagnosis: (1) Supabase audit confirmed Karen&rsquo;s data IS intact under user_id <code>ecf8bcee-24a6-4a4d-a5f4-381166ca57fc</code> / email <code>karen.rejuv@gmail.com</code> in tenant <code>34834bcc-dbed-4e7c-99b1-8f4198fc739b</code> (slug=rejuv, is_demo=false) &mdash; 1140 patient rows present. The &lsquo;Rejuv Skin Spa&rsquo; in the PersonaSwitcher dropdown was a demo seed tenant (<code>decaffaa-0000-0000-0000-00000000000a</code>, slug=rejuv-demo, is_demo=true) owned by the synthetic <code>decaffaa-0000-0000-0000-000000000001</code> seed user with email <code>testspaowner@test.com</code> &mdash; only 1 patient. Two tenants with identical display names, only one visible. (2) A tenant-rename earlier in the session (demo tenant &rarr; &lsquo;Rejuv Skin Spa (Demo)&rsquo;) failed to surface Karen&rsquo;s real tenant. That eliminated the &lsquo;display-name dedup&rsquo; hypothesis and pointed to a filter, not a dedup. <strong>The root cause</strong>: <code>src/lib/personas.ts</code> defines a hardcoded allowlist <code>DEMO_PERSONA_EMAILS</code> that PersonaSwitcher uses to narrow the listImpersonableUsers result. The allowlist is derived from <code>PERSONA_EMAILS.karen</code> which still points at <code>testspaowner@test.com</code> &mdash; the demo seed email. v1.28.0&rsquo;s rename of dormantspaowner@test.com &rarr; karen.rejuv@gmail.com (the keystone Karen-Mac iMessage MCP ship that promoted Karen&rsquo;s dormant tenant to her real prod login) never propagated to this allowlist. The exact footgun v1.26.17 was supposed to close (single source of truth for persona emails) &mdash; but only for renames that affect both public mint AND admin dropdown. v1.28.0 was a tenant-identity promotion that touched neither file. <strong>The fix</strong>: NOT a one-line value swap on <code>PERSONA_EMAILS.karen</code>, because that const is ALSO consumed by <code>src/server/v417-persona-mint.ts</code> for the public <code>/personas</code> magic-link mint flow &mdash; pointing public mint at <code>karen.rejuv@gmail.com</code> would let anonymous visitors mint magic-links into Karen&rsquo;s real production account. Security regression. Instead: new constant <code>ADMIN_VIEWABLE_REAL_EMAILS</code> (a separate Set) holds real-but-admin-viewable emails. <code>DEMO_PERSONA_EMAILS</code> derives from <code>PERSONA_EMAILS + DEMO_PERSONA_KEYS</code> PLUS <code>ADMIN_VIEWABLE_REAL_EMAILS</code>, so PersonaSwitcher sees Karen&rsquo;s real account but the public mint flow does NOT. Architectural separation between &lsquo;who is admin-viewable&rsquo; (PersonaSwitcher) and &lsquo;who is publicly mint-able&rsquo; (PERSONA_EMAILS). Adding the email is one entry in the new Set. <strong>Net effect</strong>: PersonaSwitcher dropdown will now show TWO Spa Owner entries &mdash; &lsquo;Rejuv Skin Spa&rsquo; (Karen&rsquo;s real tenant under karen.rejuv@gmail.com) and &lsquo;Rejuv Skin Spa (Demo)&rsquo; (the testspaowner@test.com demo seed). Picking the real one lands Grasshopper on her actual 1,140-patient roster + 217-row catalog + the soft-tag work from earlier session. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: the broader pattern of v1.x.0 ships that touch auth.users.email without checking the personas.ts allowlist &mdash; needs a feedback memory bank (queued: <code>feedback_persona_allowlist_after_auth_rename</code>). The catalog &lsquo;0 products&rsquo; observation from the audit was a false alarm: catalog data lives in dedicated <code>catalog_products</code> + <code>catalog_services</code> tables, not <code>knowledge_nodes</code> (my Q4 diagnostic was wrong table). Karen&rsquo;s real 217 catalog rows are intact and will appear once she lands on the right tenant. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/lib/personas.ts</code> (new ADMIN_VIEWABLE_REAL_EMAILS Set with karen.rejuv@gmail.com, DEMO_PERSONA_EMAILS spreads both DEMO_PERSONA_KEYS-derived + the new admin-viewable set), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration, no schema change, no security regression.",
