      "<strong>v1.34.1 &mdash; Coherency pass. Before riffing forward into Recognition Engine v1.34.2, a deliberate stop-and-scan ship to make sure the v1.31-v1.34 feature wave has navigation, visual consistency, and discoverability.</strong> &ldquo;Amazing features + no map&rdquo; was the riff-coding trap from prior sessions; the Wishlist + Soft-Tags + Life Events + Purchase Patterns + Bulk-Apply all landed fast across one evening and risked the same. This ship is the receipt &mdash; four coherency gaps closed in one pass before the next strategic moat ship lands on top. <strong>Slice 1 &mdash; Promos chip promoted into RefillNav</strong>: <code>/app/refill/promos</code> has existed as a route since the v341 port from openagenticv4 but never had a nav chip &mdash; an entire feature (manufacturer promos matched to the spa&rsquo;s catalog via service-manufacturer eligibility) was undiscoverable from the spa-side nav. Now appears between Catalog and Recovery in the &lsquo;data primitives&rsquo; cluster (Patients = WHO, Catalog = WHAT we sell, Promos = WHAT manufacturers offer). <code>RefillNavKey</code> union extended, <code>deriveActiveKey</code> in <code>RefillShellChrome</code> updated so the chip highlights when the route is active. <strong>Slice 2 &mdash; Soft-tag filter chip strip on patient list</strong>: v1.34.0 shipped bulk soft-tag apply (Karen can tag 50 patients at once) but the list page had zero way to filter back to who&rsquo;s tagged what &mdash; structural asymmetry. Now: a new chip strip renders below the manufacturer filter whenever at least one tag has been applied in the tenant. One chip per (tag-key, value) tuple that appears on a real patient &mdash; seeded tags (Loyal, Specials seeker, High income, etc.) AND tenant-wide custom tag-def values (Galderma Loyalist, A-list Snowbird, etc.). Multi-select union semantics: clicking multiple chips shows patients matching ANY of them. Count badges per chip show how many patients have that specific value. Clear link appears when filters are active. Most-used chips surface first (sorted by count desc). Helper functions added: <code>patientTagFilterKeys</code> (enumerate a patient&rsquo;s filter-keys including seeded + custom selections, excluding free-text culturalNotes), <code>tagFilterKeyLabel</code> (resolve a filter-key to a display label including custom-def name lookup), <code>SEEDED_TAG_VALUE_LABELS</code> map (compact list-friendly labels distinct from the patient-detail page&rsquo;s richer renderings). New state: <code>softTagFilter: Set&lt;string&gt;</code>. New useMemo: <code>softTagCounts</code> (window-aware enumeration of active filter-key tuples). Filter logic threaded into the existing <code>filtered</code> useMemo with union check. <strong>Slice 3 &mdash; Tag pill cluster on each patient row</strong>: previously the list rows had ZERO indication of which patients were tagged; Karen had to drill into each detail page to find out. Now: a small inline <code>SoftTagPillCluster</code> renders below the displayName + overdue/banned chips in the Patient cell. Shows up to 2 tag pills (emerald-soft chip style matching the detail page) + a &lsquo;+N more&rsquo; overflow indicator when the patient has more than 2 tags. Title attribute on the cluster shows all tag labels space-separated for hover discoverability without expanding the row. Order matches the patient detail page card sequence (loyalty &rarr; specials &rarr; income &rarr; negotiator &rarr; personality &rarr; custom). Cultural notes intentionally skipped (free-text doesn&rsquo;t fit chip semantics). <code>customDefs</code> threaded through <code>PatientRow</code> props so per-row lookups for custom-def names are O(1) over the small defs array without re-fetching. <strong>Slice 4 &mdash; RefillHome dashboard parity with nav</strong>: dashboard quick-actions grid (5 cards: Patients/Recovery/Inbox/Settings/Billing) didn&rsquo;t match the nav chip strip (which had Catalog as a 6th chip since v1.29.2 + now Promos as the 7th from Slice 1). Visual contract broken &mdash; new Karen would see one mental model in nav, a different one on the dashboard. Now: dashboard cards = 7 cards = 7 nav chips, same order, same labels. Catalog (BookOpen icon, &lsquo;Services and products you offer&rsquo;) and Promos (Sparkles icon, &lsquo;Manufacturer offers matched to your catalog&rsquo;) added. Grid changed from <code>lg:grid-cols-5</code> to <code>lg:grid-cols-4</code> for a balanced 4+3 split on desktop (7 cards in a 5-col grid wraps awkwardly). <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong> (deferred to dedicated future ships per Grasshopper&rsquo;s triage): the 3,451-line patient detail page + SoftTagsCard mega-container with 3 nested CRUD layers (needs its own surgical refactor); legacy per-patient custom tags from v1.31.1 deprecation banner + migration UI (isolated, lands in a v1.34.2.x sweep); the orphan-route inventory (Campaigns / Health / Reports / Rescue / Sharing / Waitlist / Appointments &mdash; need to confirm which are intentional deep-link tools vs nav gaps before sweeping); life-event decay history audit trail (low priority). <strong>Strategic anchor</strong>: per Grasshopper&rsquo;s prior-session feedback, &ldquo;riff coding&rdquo; produces amazing-feature-no-coherency outcomes. This ship operationalizes scout-first / Boris best-practice plan-first at the multi-feature level: stop, audit, fix, then move forward. Recognition Engine becomes v1.34.2 with a clean substrate underneath. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/components/refill/RefillNav.tsx</code> (RefillNavKey union extended with &lsquo;promos&rsquo;, ITEMS array gains Promos entry between Catalog and Recovery), <code>src/components/refill/RefillShellChrome.tsx</code> (deriveActiveKey adds /app/refill/promos &rarr; &lsquo;promos&rsquo; mapping), <code>src/components/refill/RefillHome.tsx</code> (BookOpen + Sparkles icon imports, ACTIONS array gains Catalog + Promos entries in nav order, grid changed to lg:grid-cols-4 for 4+3 desktop layout), <code>src/routes/app.refill.patients.index.tsx</code> (PatientSoftTags type import + SEEDED_TAG_VALUE_LABELS map + patientTagFilterKeys helper + tagFilterKeyLabel helper + softTagFilter state + softTagCounts useMemo + filter logic in filtered useMemo + soft-tag chip strip rendered after manufacturer strip with multi-select chips and Clear affordance + SoftTagPillCluster component for per-row tag pill rendering with 2-visible-plus-overflow + customDefs prop threaded through PatientRow), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no new dependencies; no schema change.",
