      "<strong>v1.31.5 &mdash; Custom tags become TENANT-WIDE definitions, not per-patient. Set tag affordance per patient matches seeded six exactly.</strong> Per Grasshopper&rsquo;s callout while creating &lsquo;Rescheduler&rsquo; with Chronic / Occasional / Never chips on one patient: that tag should appear on EVERY patient in the practice, just like the seeded six (Income tier, Negotiator, etc.). v1.31.4 stored custom tags per-patient &mdash; wrong shape. v1.31.5 fixes the architecture: Karen defines a tag once for her practice; it appears on every patient with a Set tag affordance; per-patient she picks which chips apply (or leaves Not set). <strong>What ships</strong>: (1) New <code>CustomTagDefinition</code> type stored as <code>knowledge_nodes</code> rows with <code>node_type=&lsquo;custom_tag_definition&rsquo;</code>, <code>context=&lsquo;soft_tag_definitions&rsquo;</code>, attachments holding the chip options array. Tenant-scoped via user_id like every other knowledge_node row. Lookup_key = lowercase(name) for dedupe-by-name. (2) New <code>PatientCustomTagValue</code> shape on <code>softTags.customSelections</code> &mdash; a <code>Record&lt;definitionId, {selected[], setByUserId, setAt, reason}&gt;</code>. Chip options come from the tenant definition; the patient&rsquo;s selected subset + provenance live here. (3) Six new server fns: <code>listCustomTagDefinitions</code>, <code>createCustomTagDefinition</code> (dedupes by name &mdash; if a def with this name exists, merges new options into existing one), <code>updateCustomTagDefinition</code>, <code>deleteCustomTagDefinition</code>, <code>setPatientCustomSelection</code>, <code>clearPatientCustomSelection</code>. All threaded through <code>resolveEffectiveUserId</code> for admin viewAs. (4) <code>PatientDetail</code> shape extended with <code>customTagDefinitions: CustomTagDefinition[]</code>; <code>getPatientById</code> fetches both patient and tenant definitions in one round trip. (5) <strong>UI overhaul</strong> of SoftTagsCard: new <code>TenantCustomTagsSection</code> renders one row per definition exactly like the seeded six (uppercase label + Set tag pill OR active chips with Edit + clear). New <code>CustomSelectionForm</code> chip-picker matches preset tag UX. New <code>DefinitionEditForm</code> handles both Create-new and Edit-existing (rename + change chip options + Delete-for-all-patients with confirm). Pencil icon next to each definition opens the def editor. &lsquo;+ Create a new custom tag (shows on all patients)&rsquo; button at the bottom. After creating, the Set tag form auto-opens so Karen can immediately apply it to this patient. (6) <strong>Legacy v1.31.4 custom tags</strong> still render in a small amber-tinted &lsquo;Legacy (per-patient) custom tags &middot; pre-v1.31.5&rsquo; subsection below the tenant-wide section, with a note explaining they were created per-patient and inviting Karen to re-create them as tenant-wide tags. Existing Family/Friends Pricing + Rescheduler will appear there, editable / deletable in their old form; Karen can re-create them via the new flow in &lt;30s each, then delete the legacy entries. <strong>What this unblocks</strong>: every spa-owner&rsquo;s editorial framework (their per-practice taxonomy of patient signals) lives in one tenant-scoped definition store. Karen&rsquo;s Rescheduler / Allergies / Family-Pricing / Preferred-Day / VIP-Tier / etc. all become first-class soft tags that compose with the seeded six. The Profitability Engine scoring layer can read any tenant-defined tag the same way it reads the seeded ones. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: cross-tenant tag definition sharing (e.g., &lsquo;most spas track Rescheduler&rsquo; &mdash; future ship could surface community-seeded tag suggestions). Tag-definition history (rename or option-change overwrites in place; older option labels disappear from new patient renders if a chip is removed even if some patients had it selected). Bulk-set affordance (set the same tag value on many patients at once &mdash; future ship). Tag-definition icon / color customization. Per-role visibility (still owner-only by default). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/lib/patient-csv.ts</code> (PatientCustomTagValue + CustomTagDefinition types + customSelections field on PatientSoftTags), <code>src/server/patient-ingest.functions.ts</code> (imports + 6 new server fns + hydrateCustomTagDefinition helper + getPatientById fetches definitions + PatientDetail extended), <code>src/routes/app.refill.patients.$patientId.tsx</code> (SoftTagsCard accepts definitions + onDefinitionsChange props + new TenantCustomTagsSection + DefinitionRow + CustomSelectionForm + DefinitionEditForm + Plus icon for create button + legacy section gated on customs.length and re-labeled as Legacy with amber chrome), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no nav change. <code>knowledge_nodes.node_type</code> is free-form text so the new <code>custom_tag_definition</code> type slots in without a schema change.",
