      "<strong>v1.29.3 &mdash; Service-Products linkage + auto-COGS derive: the structural payoff of the Catalog substrate.</strong> Karen enters her products once + her services once + the math composes itself. Three things ship together: (1) the linkage UI inside the service edit form, (2) the Manual/Auto-COGS toggle, (3) a small UX consistency fix where the Products form now puts Sales price BEFORE Cost (matches the Services form ordering Grasshopper preferred). <strong>Linkage UI (the main ship)</strong>: inline section inside any service&rsquo;s edit card &mdash; &ldquo;Products consumed&rdquo; subsection that lists each linked product as a row (brand + cost/unit + editable quantity + remove). At top: Manual/Auto toggle. At bottom: an Add-product form (dropdown of unlinked products in the tenant&rsquo;s catalog + qty input + Link button). Real-time computed sum line below the list shows <code>SUM(product.cost_per_unit × quantity_per_service)</code> with an &ldquo;Active&rdquo; chip when in Auto mode. <strong>Auto-COGS semantic</strong>: when Karen flips to Auto, server computes the sum and writes it to <code>services.cogs_per_service</code>, sets <code>cogs_source = &apos;derived&apos;</code>. Every subsequent link / unlink / quantity-change on that service triggers a re-sync via <code>syncDerivedCogsIfNeeded</code>. The COGS field in the form is disabled and visually distinct (emerald background) when auto-derive is active &mdash; clear visual signal that &ldquo;this number is being managed for you.&rdquo; Toggle back to Manual leaves the current derived value as the starting point Karen can edit. Pre-flight: Auto button is disabled until at least one product is linked. <strong>UX consistency fix</strong>: Products form now reads Sales price &rarr; Cost per unit (same order as Services form). Both the form inputs AND the card-row display flipped to &ldquo;<code>$X sell &middot; $Y cost</code>&rdquo;. Karen learns one mental order across both surfaces. <strong>New server fns in <code>refill-catalog.ts</code></strong>: <code>listServiceProductsFn</code> (returns service + links bundle), <code>linkProductToServiceFn</code> (upsert on the unique service_id+product_id constraint so re-linking the same product updates quantity), <code>updateServiceProductQuantityFn</code>, <code>unlinkServiceProductFn</code>, <code>setServiceCogsSourceFn</code>. Each mutation that touches linkage on a derived-mode service auto-recomputes and persists the new cogs_per_service. Defense-in-depth: every fn re-validates that both joined service AND product belong to the caller&rsquo;s tenant. <strong>Architectural notes</strong>: (1) Recomputation is app-side, not Postgres-trigger-based &mdash; keeps the migration footprint small and makes the derive logic visible in TypeScript. Trade-off: when a product&rsquo;s <code>cost_per_unit</code> changes via Products CRUD, dependent services in derived mode have stale COGS until the next time Karen touches the linkage. v1.29.4 candidate to add a &ldquo;Refresh derived COGS&rdquo; sweep that re-runs across all derived services on cost change. (2) Linkage UI only renders in edit mode &mdash; a service must exist before it can have linked products (no link-during-create flow). (3) Products list is fetched once on services-page mount, parallel with services fetch, so the dropdown is hot when Karen enters edit mode. <strong>Verification walk</strong>: ensure at least one product exists at <code>/catalog/products</code> (Botox vial $400 cost / $1200 sell) &rarr; navigate to <code>/catalog/services</code> &rarr; add a service &ldquo;Botox / unit&rdquo; price $14 with COGS blank &rarr; click to edit &rarr; Products consumed section renders &ldquo;No products linked yet&rdquo; &rarr; pick Botox vial from the dropdown + qty <code>0.01</code> (assuming the vial is 100 units) + Link &rarr; row appears showing Botox · $400/vial · 0.01 · $4.00 contribution &rarr; flip to Auto &rarr; COGS field disables and shows <code>4.00</code> &rarr; margin updates to <code>$10.00 (71%)</code>. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: no &ldquo;refresh derived COGS&rdquo; sweep when product costs change (queued). No bulk-link UI. No tenant-customizable categories. No CSV import (v1.29.4). <strong>Rollback</strong>: <code>git revert</code>; no DB damage (service_products table already exists from v1.29.0; derived COGS values are recomputable). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/server/refill-catalog.ts</code> (extended with linkage types + 5 new server fns + computeDerivedCogs + syncDerivedCogsIfNeeded helpers), <code>src/routes/app.refill.catalog.services.tsx</code> (rewritten to include linkage UI inline in edit form + LinkageSection + LinkRow components), <code>src/routes/app.refill.catalog.products.tsx</code> (form field order swap + card row text flip), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no nav change.",
