      "<strong>v1.29.2 &mdash; Services CRUD + Catalog chip lifted into RefillNav.</strong> Two things land together: the Services UI mirror of v1.29.1 Products, AND the Catalog chip surfaced as the second nav chip (after Patients, before Recovery). <strong>Nav decision reversal</strong>: the v1.29.0/.1 changelogs said catalog stays deep-link-only per <code>project_refill_trojan_horse_thesis</code>. After v1.29.1 walked clean, Grasshopper called it &mdash; the trojan-horse thesis is about PUBLIC-facing positioning (landing / scan / onboard), not the authenticated nav Karen sees after logging in. Hiding daily-use surfaces behind deep links makes her work harder for no positioning benefit. Slot: Patients (WHO data) &rarr; Catalog (WHAT data) &rarr; Recovery (action) &rarr; Inbox (comms) &rarr; Settings (config) &rarr; Billing (back-office). The chip routes to <code>/app/refill/catalog/products</code> by default; the products / services routes are siblings under <code>/catalog</code>. <strong>Services UI (the main ship)</strong>: mirror of v1.29.1 Products against the <code>services</code> table. Surface at <code>/app/refill/catalog/services</code>. <strong>What lands</strong>: extended <code>src/server/refill-catalog.ts</code> with four service server fns &mdash; <code>listServicesFn</code>, <code>createServiceFn</code>, <code>updateServiceFn</code>, <code>deleteServiceFn</code>. Same auth pattern verbatim (verifyAuth &rarr; resolveEffectiveUserId &rarr; getTenantIdForUser). <strong>UI</strong>: <code>src/routes/app.refill.catalog.services.tsx</code> mirrors the products page shape: grouped by category, one card per service, click to edit in place, inline add expander, delete with confirm, empty-state CTA. <strong>Key differences from products</strong>: (1) service categories diverge from product categories per the v1.29.0 migration &mdash; services have <code>laser</code> + <code>facial</code> (treatment categories), products have <code>laser_consumable</code> (product category); (2) <code>cogs_per_service</code> is NULLABLE &mdash; Karen can enter a service with sales price only and leave COGS blank now, v1.29.3 will auto-derive COGS from the product linkage; (3) when COGS is null, the row renders &ldquo;Set COGS for margin&rdquo; instead of the margin number; (4) cogs_source flag stamped to <code>manual</code> on create / update (v1.29.3 introduces the <code>derived</code> path); (5) services have no manufacturer column (manufacturer attribution lives on products only, flows through linkage). <strong>UX detail</strong>: the COGS field placeholder reads &ldquo;Leave blank to auto-derive in v1.29.3&rdquo; &mdash; signals the upcoming feature without forcing immediate entry. <strong>What this unblocks</strong>: v1.29.3 service_products linkage UI + auto-derive toggle that rewrites cogs_per_service from <code>SUM(product.cost_per_unit × quantity_per_service)</code> and flips cogs_source to <code>derived</code>. v1.29.4 Acuity CSV import (validated against Karen&rsquo;s real export). <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: no auto-derive yet (v1.29.3). No linkage UI yet (v1.29.3). No nav-chip widening per <code>project_refill_trojan_horse_thesis</code>. No CSV import. No bulk-edit. <strong>Verification</strong>: log in &rarr; navigate to <code>/app/refill/catalog/services</code> &rarr; empty state renders &rarr; add &ldquo;Botox treatment / unit&rdquo; (Tox category, price $14, leave COGS blank) &rarr; row renders with &ldquo;Set COGS for margin&rdquo; chip &rarr; edit &rarr; set COGS to $6.50 &rarr; save &rarr; row renders with $7.50 (54%) margin. <strong>Rollback</strong>: <code>git revert</code>; no DB damage (services table already exists from v1.29.0). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/server/refill-catalog.ts</code> (extended with services types + four service fns + ServiceRow shape adapter), <code>src/routes/app.refill.catalog.services.tsx</code> (new file, ~450 lines), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no nav change.",
