      "<strong>v1.29.0 &mdash; Product Catalog schema: the substrate primitive the entire Profitability Engine depends on.</strong> Spec authored 2026-06-01 at <code>Desktop/Refill-Profitability-Engine-Spec-v0_1.html</code> &mdash; this ship implements §3.1 (the catalog primitive) of the consolidated substrate-plus-engines architecture. <strong>Why this comes first</strong>: every downstream piece &mdash; margin-aware patient profitability scoring, brand-affinity matching for the Recognition Allocation Engine, combo-treatment detection, manufacturer-rebate-tier compounding &mdash; depends on knowing per-product cost / sales-price / margin and per-service COGS. Without the catalog, the 17-factor scoring engine cannot compute factor #1 (gross margin per visit) and the Recognition Engine cannot route Allergan rebates to Allergan-product patients. <strong>What shipped</strong>: <code>supabase/migrations/20260601020000_v1_29_0_product_catalog.sql</code> &mdash; three tables: <code>public.products</code> (per-tenant physical product rows with brand / category / unit_type / cost_per_unit / sales_price_per_unit / manufacturer), <code>public.services</code> (per-tenant service rows with name / category / service_price / cogs_per_service / cogs_source), and <code>public.service_products</code> (many-to-many junction with quantity_per_service for combo-treatment math). Plus <code>set_updated_at</code> trigger (idempotent <code>create or replace</code>), indexes on tenant_id / category / manufacturer, RLS enabled with service-role-only policies (matches the refill_pricing_plans / refill_invoices pattern). <strong>Architectural calls (CTO, 2026-06-01)</strong>: (1) text + CHECK constraint over Postgres ENUM &mdash; matches every modern tenant-scoped table; (2) RLS service-role-only &mdash; matches the established Phase-1.6+ pattern; (3) manufacturer values unified with <code>src/lib/product-manufacturer-map.ts</code> TS enum (abbvie / galderma / evolus / merz / skinceuticals / eltamd / neocutis / obagi / revance / rha / sciton / abbvie-coolsculpting) plus <code>generic</code> + <code>in_house</code> for the long tail &mdash; note Allergan → AbbVie because AbbVie owns the brand post-2020 and the existing TS map already encodes it; (4) <code>cogs_per_service</code> nullable + <code>cogs_source</code> flag (default <code>manual</code>) so v1.29.3 auto-derive can rewrite the scalar from linkage sum and flip the flag without breaking the read path. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: no CRUD UI yet (v1.29.1 Products, v1.29.2 Services, v1.29.3 linkage). No CSV import yet (v1.29.4, validated against Karen&rsquo;s real Acuity service-list export per <code>feedback_validate_against_real_exports</code>). No price-history ledger (deferred &mdash; current state in cost_per_unit / sales_price_per_unit columns only). No tenant-customizable categories (hard-coded at v1.x.0; revisit when spa #2 onboarding surfaces a category gap). No nav-chip widening (per <code>project_refill_trojan_horse_thesis</code> the 5-chip RefillNav stays narrow forever; catalog is deep-link-only at v1.29.0). <strong>Rollback</strong>: drop in reverse FK order &mdash; <code>drop table public.service_products; drop table public.services; drop table public.products;</code> (the <code>set_updated_at</code> function stays in place; harmless if other tables use it). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>supabase/migrations/20260601020000_v1_29_0_product_catalog.sql</code> (new file, the migration), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). Pure data ship; no worker-code change. v1.29.1 Products CRUD lands the first UI surface against this schema.",
