    items: [
      "<strong>v1.26.17 &mdash; Collapse persona-mint roster and PersonaSwitcher allowlist onto a single source of truth.</strong> Pre-v1.26.17 there were two files defining who the demo personas are, with no enforcement that they stay aligned. <code>src/server/v417-persona-mint.ts</code> held <code>PERSONA_EMAILS</code> = { admin, kelly, maria, karen } — the 4-key map the public /personas page resolves at magic-link mint time. <code>src/lib/demo-personas.ts</code> held <code>DEMO_PERSONA_EMAILS</code> = Set&lt;{karen-email, kelly-email}&gt; — the email allowlist the admin PersonaSwitcher uses to filter <code>listImpersonableUsers</code>. The two overlap on karen + kelly (both consumers see the same person), but the karen + kelly emails were duplicated as string literals across both files. v1.26.13&rsquo;s Karen tenant rename (<code>karen@rejuv-demo.test</code> &rarr; <code>testspaowner@test.com</code>) had to manually edit both files to keep them aligned. Miss one and the public /personas mint and the admin dropdown drift &mdash; admin sees a tenant in the dropdown that can&rsquo;t be minted, or vice versa. The bug was dormant after v1.26.13 (both were edited correctly), but the architecture was a footgun waiting for the next rename. <strong>Compounding</strong>: <code>v417-persona-mint.ts</code>&rsquo;s docblock pointed at <code>src/server/v417-personas.ts</code> as the alignment source-of-truth, but that file doesn&rsquo;t exist (stale comment from a never-built future state). <strong>Fix</strong>: new <code>src/lib/personas.ts</code> &mdash; client-safe pure-const module &mdash; holds <code>PERSONA_EMAILS</code> + <code>PersonaKey</code> + <code>DEMO_PERSONA_KEYS</code> (subset of personas surfaced in the admin dropdown) + <code>DEMO_PERSONA_EMAILS</code> (computed from the previous two; what PersonaSwitcher actually consumes). <code>v417-persona-mint.ts</code> drops its local <code>PERSONA_EMAILS</code> declaration + the long alignment-history docblock and imports the constant from <code>@/lib/personas</code>; re-exports <code>PersonaKey</code> for back-compat with downstream callers that may have been importing it from the server file. <code>PersonaSwitcher.tsx</code> import line flips from <code>@/lib/demo-personas</code> &rarr; <code>@/lib/personas</code>; consumer code unchanged. <code>src/lib/demo-personas.ts</code> deleted entirely (zero remaining consumers after the flip). <strong>Why client-safe lib not server file</strong>: PersonaSwitcher is client code and can&rsquo;t import from a file that uses <code>createServerFn</code> + service-role admin client without dragging server deps into the browser bundle. Pure-const lib module is the canonical shape. <strong>Why DEMO_PERSONA_KEYS separate from DEMO_PERSONA_EMAILS</strong>: the keys are the deliberate product call (per Grasshopper&rsquo;s v1.24.4 three-personas directive: Admin excluded as &lsquo;caller&rsquo;, Maria excluded as &lsquo;not in the canonical walk&rsquo;); the emails are mechanically derived. Adding a 4th visible persona is editing the keys set, not duplicating email strings. <strong>Net effect</strong>: next persona rename touches exactly one place. The footgun is closed. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/lib/personas.ts</code> (new file, the canonical source), <code>src/server/v417-persona-mint.ts</code> (PERSONA_EMAILS removed, import + type re-export added), <code>src/components/admin/PersonaSwitcher.tsx</code> (import flip), <code>src/lib/demo-personas.ts</code> (deleted), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
    ],
