      "<strong>v1.26.14 &mdash; Kill four dead billing fns flagged in v1.26.7/.8.</strong> The v1.7.2 emma&harr;refill UI unification routed <code>app.billing.tsx</code> to <code>refill-billing.ts</code> for plan + invoice fns, leaving the emma-billing equivalents (<code>applyPricingPlan</code>, <code>getActivePlan</code>, <code>listInvoices</code>) with zero call sites. Mirror situation on the recovery dashboard: <code>app.refill.recovery.tsx</code> imports <code>getInvoicePreview</code> from <code>emma-billing.functions.ts</code>, so the <code>refill-billing.ts</code> variant was the dead one. v1.26.7/.8 audits identified all four and explicitly punted to a separate cleanup ship (the note read &lsquo;dead and intentionally NOT fixed in this sweep &mdash; separate cleanup ship should decide delete-vs-migrate&rsquo;). This is that ship. <strong>Removed from <code>src/server/emma-billing.functions.ts</code></strong>: <code>applyPricingPlan</code> server fn + <code>applyPlanInput</code> zod schema. <code>getActivePlan</code> server fn. <code>listInvoices</code> server fn + <code>accessTokenOnly</code> zod schema (was shared by the two dead fns). <code>ActivePlan</code> + <code>Invoice</code> exported types (orphaned after fn removal; refill-billing&rsquo;s <code>RefillActivePlan</code>/<code>RefillInvoice</code> are the live equivalents). <code>verifyAuth</code> import dropped from the import line (no remaining callers in this file). <code>PricingPlan</code> type kept &mdash; still consumed by <code>getInvoicePreview</code>, <code>getPlanEconomics</code>, <code>PLAN_ECONOMICS</code>. <strong>Removed from <code>src/server/refill-billing.ts</code></strong>: <code>getInvoicePreview</code> server fn + <code>RefillInvoicePreview</code> exported type (dead since v1.7.2). <code>accessTokenOnly</code> + <code>verifyAuth</code> imports retained &mdash; both still have other live consumers in the file. <strong>Top-of-file docblocks updated</strong> in both files to reflect the removals (was listing the dead fns under &lsquo;Surfaces&rsquo; &mdash; misleading). <strong>Verification</strong>: <code>grep -rn 'applyPricingPlan\\|getActivePlan\\|listInvoices' src/</code> across non-changelog files returned only references in <code>app.billing.tsx</code> (which imports from refill-billing &mdash; the live source) and the two billing files (now only refill-billing exports them). <code>getInvoicePreview</code> grep returned only the emma-billing definition + the recovery route&rsquo;s import &mdash; both live. Worker bundle dropped from 795.35 kB &rarr; 794.55 kB confirming dead code actually removed, not just hidden by re-export chains. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: the broader emma&harr;refill unification is still on the backlog &mdash; <code>emma-billing.functions.ts</code> still owns <code>generateMonthlyInvoiceForUser</code>/<code>generateMonthlyInvoicesForAll</code> writing to the legacy <code>emma_invoices</code> table, and the <code>/api/cron/emma-invoice</code> route still calls them. That&rsquo;s a heavier migration (data table cutover, cron-route swap, idempotency-key bridge) and stays on backlog until a real reason forces it. The naming-collision discovery from v1.26.7 (both files exported identically-named fns) is now resolved structurally &mdash; only one file exports each name. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/server/emma-billing.functions.ts</code> (docblock, 1 import edit, 2 type removals, 2 schema removals, 3 fn removals), <code>src/server/refill-billing.ts</code> (docblock, 1 type removal, 1 fn removal), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
