      "<strong>v1.26.13 &mdash; Rename two Karen tenants to test-naming convention.</strong> Surfaced during the v1.26.12 verification: I (Po) repeatedly mis-identified which tenant is LIVE vs dormant because both auth emails embed the human name &lsquo;Karen&rsquo; and the `.test` suffix on `karen@rejuv-demo.test` LOOKS like dev-data when it&rsquo;s actually production-active. The 2026-05-29 diagnostic settled it: <code>karen@rejuv-demo.test</code> holds 11 rescue_attempts + 10 offers + 9 future cancellations + a configured noshow_policy + an active email proxy to <code>davidfand303@gmail.com</code> (the live-fire delivery path); <code>karen.aslak@gmail.com</code> has 5754 historical Acuity appointments + 1140 QB-uploaded patients but zero rescue activity ever. <strong>Convention shift</strong>: separate auth identity (logged-in email, robot-generic, screams &lsquo;test&rsquo;) from display name (UI + customer copy, warm human name). Auth gets <code>test{role}@test.com</code>; display name stays &lsquo;Karen&rsquo; via the v1.26.12 spa-profile <code>owner-display-name</code>. Customers texting still see &lsquo;with Karen&rsquo; — the two layers cleanly separate. <strong>Renamed</strong>: <code>karen@rejuv-demo.test</code> &rarr; <code>testspaowner@test.com</code> (LIVE working tenant — the one v417 persona-mint routes to). <code>karen.aslak@gmail.com</code> &rarr; <code>dormantspaowner@test.com</code> (holds QB roster + historical Acuity data but engine never fires there). user_ids preserved across the rename so every foreign-key reference (knowledge_nodes, emma_appointments, emma_rescue_offers, emma_reliability_status, user_roles, admin_audit_log, etc.) stays intact. <strong>Code changes</strong>: <code>src/server/v417-persona-mint.ts</code> — <code>PERSONA_EMAILS.karen</code> updated to point at <code>testspaowner@test.com</code>; public /personas page magic-link mint now routes through the renamed email. <code>src/lib/demo-personas.ts</code> — <code>DEMO_PERSONA_EMAILS</code> allowlist updated; admin PersonaSwitcher dropdown now shows the LIVE tenant instead of the dormant gmail. The v1.24.5-era choice was correct for &lsquo;where do the patients live&rsquo; but wrong for &lsquo;where does the engine fire&rsquo; — v417 superseded that for the public mint flow; this allowlist now follows for the admin flow too. <strong>SQL rename</strong>: two-statement <code>UPDATE auth.users.email</code>, pasted into Supabase dashboard by Grasshopper after this deploy lands. <strong>Memory rewrites queued</strong>: <code>project_rejuv_demo_test_tenant.md</code> (was &lsquo;active dev/test residue, defer cleanup&rsquo; — wrong on every axis; rewriting as &lsquo;LIVE working tenant, now testspaowner@test.com&rsquo;), <code>feedback_supabase_project_url.md</code> (already references both emails — needs flip), new <code>feedback_test_naming_convention.md</code> (the rule going forward). <strong>2026-06-12 scheduled routine</strong>: prompt references both old emails by name; updating via RemoteTrigger so the agent looks for the renamed tenants. <strong>Side effect</strong>: any active browser session under the old emails will need to re-login via /personas — the auth.users.email rename invalidates the refresh-token cache. Touched: <code>src/server/v417-persona-mint.ts</code>, <code>src/lib/demo-personas.ts</code>, <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
