      "<strong>v1.20.6 &mdash; Admin tenant switcher in the viewing-as banner; multi-real-tenant future-proofing.</strong> Pre-v1.20.6, <code>getFirstTenantForAdmin</code> auto-picked the first-by-ordering tenant (real-before-demo per v1.20.3) and there was no way for admin to view a different tenant short of editing localStorage by hand or running SQL. Fine for the current single-real-tenant world (just Rejuv) but breaks the moment we onboard a second pilot. v1.20.6 ships the switcher. <strong>New server fn</strong>: <code>listTenantsForAdmin</code> in <code>src/server/refill-tenants.ts</code> — same admin role re-verification as getFirstTenantForAdmin, returns every tenant in the system with its owner user_id (bulk-fetched in one round-trip from tenant_memberships, prefers role=&lsquo;owner&rsquo; rows, falls back to first membership when role enum is unpopulated). Sorted real-before-demo + created_at ASC within each group so the dropdown matches the default-selection ordering admin already sees. <strong>Extended server fn</strong>: <code>getFirstTenantForAdmin</code> takes optional <code>preferredTenantId</code>. When set + tenant exists, returns that tenant + its owner instead of the default first-by-ordering. Falls through to the v1.20.3 ordering when preferred tenant doesn&rsquo;t exist (defensive against stale localStorage from deleted tenants — won&rsquo;t throw, just picks a sensible default). <strong>Persistence layer</strong>: <code>src/lib/use-tenant-membership.ts</code> exports <code>ADMIN_VIEW_AS_TENANT_ID_KEY</code> + <code>setAdminViewAsTenantId(tenantId)</code>. The hook reads localStorage on the admin-fallback path and passes the value as <code>preferredTenantId</code>. The setter writes the new id and triggers a full <code>window.location.reload()</code> &mdash; not a SPA-style re-render, because invalidating the use-tenant-membership cache + every page-side viewAsUserId effect that&rsquo;s already plumbed would be complex and easy to miss; a reload is one line and unambiguously correct (full re-mount of all components with fresh viewAsUserId). <strong>UI</strong>: <code>RefillShellChrome</code> fetches the tenant list when <code>viewAs === \"admin\"</code> and renders an inline native <code>&lt;select&gt;</code> in the banner replacing the static tenant name. Dropdown shows each tenant name with &lsquo;(demo)&rsquo; suffix on is_demo tenants so admin doesn&rsquo;t accidentally view-as a seed thinking it&rsquo;s real. When there&rsquo;s only one tenant (today&rsquo;s single-Rejuv world ignoring rejuv-demo), the dropdown falls back to a static <code>&lt;strong&gt;</code> — no useless picker. On change, calls <code>setAdminViewAsTenantId</code> which writes localStorage + reloads → entire app re-mounts with the new viewing-as context, including all v1.20 viewAsUserId-plumbed data fetchers. <strong>UX decision rationale</strong>: native select over Popover/custom dropdown because (a) zero extra deps, (b) keyboard navigation + accessibility free, (c) inline-in-text reads naturally (&lsquo;Viewing as [Rejuv ▾] (admin fallback)&rsquo;), (d) reload-on-change is the simplest correct refresh path. Touched: <code>src/server/refill-tenants.ts</code> (listTenantsForAdmin + getFirstTenantForAdmin preferredTenantId), <code>src/lib/use-tenant-membership.ts</code> (localStorage helpers + preferredTenantId plumbing), <code>src/components/refill/RefillShellChrome.tsx</code> (switcher fetch + select markup), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
