      "<strong>v1.20.5 &mdash; <code>ingestPatientCsv</code> opted into the admin viewing-as write path; closes the SQL-detour footgun.</strong> v1.20 explicitly excluded all write paths from viewAs &lsquo;for safety,&rsquo; but the 2026-05-27 Rejuv pilot upload immediately surfaced the cost of that policy: Grasshopper uploaded the real Rejuv CSV while signed in as admin (viewing-as the tenant in chrome), and the rows landed under his admin user_id instead of the tenant&rsquo;s owner. Required a manual <code>Patient-Data-Move-To-Karen.sql</code> reassign to fix. v1.20.5 narrows the original policy: <strong>ingest IS safe to viewAs</strong> because (a) the use case is explicit (admin pasting a CSV on behalf of a tenant during pilot setup), (b) <code>resolveEffectiveUserId</code> re-verifies admin role server-side before honoring the override, (c) bad ingests are reversible via the same UI. Stripe-mutating writes and plan changes are still intentionally NOT viewAs-aware. <strong>Server change</strong>: <code>ingestInput</code> gains optional <code>viewAsUserId: z.string().uuid().optional()</code>; handler swaps <code>verifyAuth(data.accessToken)</code> for <code>resolveEffectiveUserId({ accessToken, viewAsUserId })</code> and passes <code>effectiveUserId</code> to <code>doIngest</code>. Single 8-line diff; no separate <code>ingestPatientCsvAsTenant</code> fn needed (avoids the code duplication the original sketch implied). <strong>Page-side change</strong>: <code>app.refill.patients.import.tsx</code> imports <code>useTenantMembership</code>, derives <code>viewAsUserId</code> from the state, plumbs it into the <code>ingestPatientCsv</code> call. <strong>Safety surface added</strong>: when admin is viewing-as, the import page renders an amber notice (<code>Uploading into &lt;Tenant&gt;. Patients and transactions will land in this tenant&rsquo;s bucket, not yours.</code>) above the dropzone — eliminates the &lsquo;wait, where did my upload go&rsquo; surprise. <strong>Banner copy refreshed</strong>: <code>RefillShellChrome</code>&rsquo;s admin viewing-as banner updated from &lsquo;Writes still scope to your own user_id&rsquo; (stale post-v1.20.5) to &lsquo;CSV ingest writes into this tenant (v1.20.5). Stripe and plan writes still scope to your own user_id&rsquo; — accurate, narrow callout of which writes are safe to viewAs. <strong>While in the file</strong>: also swept the Emma user-facing strings (eyebrow, description, breadcrumbs) per <em>feedback-emma-never-user-facing</em> — &lsquo;Emma(OS) · Patients&rsquo; &rarr; &lsquo;Refill · Patients&rsquo;, &lsquo;Emma turns it into&rsquo; &rarr; &lsquo;Refill turns it into&rsquo;. Touched: <code>src/server/patient-ingest.functions.ts</code> (zod + handler), <code>src/routes/app.refill.patients.import.tsx</code> (page plumbing + viewing-as notice + Emma sweep), <code>src/components/refill/RefillShellChrome.tsx</code> (banner copy), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
