      "<strong>v1.20.4 &mdash; Admin-bypass path was dead since v1.19, fixed.</strong> Discovered during the post-v1.20.3 walk-through: the v1.19 <code>useTenantMembership</code> admin-fallback was gated on <code>primaryRole === \"admin\"</code> from <code>useAuth()</code>. But <code>useAuth().primaryRole</code> reads <code>user_preferences.primary_role</code> &mdash; the shell-selection signal whose type is <code>PrimaryRole = \"spa-owner\" | \"rep\" | \"developer\"</code> per <code>src/server/user-prefs.functions.ts:26</code>. <strong>\"admin\" is not a valid PrimaryRole value &mdash; the gate could never be true.</strong> So the v1.19 admin-bypass code path was dead from the day it shipped. It looked like it worked because Grasshopper had a hack tenant_memberships row (inserted via Tenant-Membership-Grant.sql) that made <code>getMyTenant</code> return a real tenant, so the fallback was never reached. The moment that row was dropped (to test v1.20.3 ordering cleanly), <code>useTenantMembership</code> returned NOT_A_TENANT &rArr; <code>src/routes/app.tsx:112</code> failed the <code>isRefillPath &amp;&amp; tenantMembership.tenant</code> guard &rArr; rendered bare <code>&lt;Outlet&gt;</code> &rArr; RefillHome returned null &rArr; <strong>blank pages everywhere</strong>. <strong>Fix</strong>: removed the client-side gate entirely. The server fn <code>getFirstTenantForAdmin</code> already re-verifies admin role against <code>public.user_roles</code> and throws <code>\"Admin only.\"</code> for non-admins &mdash; we catch that and fall through to NOT_A_TENANT, the same end state as before. Cost: one extra POST per non-tenant non-admin sign-in returning 401. Non-tenant users are rare (typically mid-onboarding) so the bandwidth is negligible. Authoritative admin gate stays where it belongs (server-side, against user_roles, with service-role read bypassing RLS). <strong>Three SQL files dropped on Desktop during the diagnostic</strong>: <code>Admin-Drop-Rejuv-Membership.sql</code> (the drop that triggered the blank pages), <code>Admin-Restore-Rejuv-Membership.sql</code> (emergency restore so app loads again pre-fix), <code>Admin-Bypass-Diagnostic.sql</code> (4-row read-only check that cleared suspects 2+3 and pointed at suspect 1). Diagnostic confirmed: admin role row exists (1), is_demo column populated (2 rows: false=1, true=1), v1.20.3 ordering correctly picks <code>rejuv</code> (is_demo=false). <strong>Post-fix flow</strong>: admin can now drop the membership row safely. Hard refresh &rArr; <code>getMyTenant</code> returns null &rArr; v1.20.4 fallback always attempts <code>getFirstTenantForAdmin</code> &rArr; succeeds (admin role + is_demo ordering both valid) &rArr; chrome renders with admin viewing-as banner &rArr; v1.20 viewAsUserId plumbs &rArr; Karen's 1,140 patients render. Touched: <code>src/lib/use-tenant-membership.ts</code> (removed primaryRole gate + updated docblock), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
