      "<strong>v1.9 &mdash; emma&harr;refill UI unification + InvoiceRow TZ fix (closes the Frankenstein).</strong> Two small-but-load-bearing cleanups in one ship. <strong>(1) UI unification</strong>: <code>app.billing.tsx</code> finally finishes the emma&rarr;refill migration that v1.7.2 started. Imports for <code>applyPricingPlan</code>, <code>getActivePlan</code>, <code>getPlanEconomics</code>, and the associated types now come from <code>@/server/refill-billing</code> instead of <code>@/server/emma-billing.functions</code>. The page&rsquo;s state types flip from <code>ActivePlan</code> / <code>PricingPlan</code> to <code>RefillActivePlan</code> / <code>RefillPricingPlan</code>, and <code>PLAN_META</code> re-keys from <code>performance</code>/<code>predictable</code>/<code>hybrid</code> to the canonical <code>starter</code>/<code>predictable</code>/<code>pro</code>. <strong>The visible plan labels stay the same</strong> (&ldquo;Performance&rdquo; / &ldquo;Predictable&rdquo; / &ldquo;Hybrid&rdquo;) so Karen&rsquo;s mental model isn&rsquo;t disturbed by an internal refactor &mdash; a future copy-refresh ship can rename if the marketing story shifts. Dropped: the v1.7.2 <code>refillPlanToUiPlan</code> mapper that translated between the two key spaces (no longer needed &mdash; <code>PLAN_META</code> keys are the refill names directly). The chain-break that bit us in tonight&rsquo;s v1.7.x walks &mdash; &ldquo;click Pick Performance &rarr; cron picks up Karen&rdquo; was wrong because the UI wrote to <code>emma_pricing_plans</code> while the cron read <code>refill_pricing_plans</code> &mdash; is now structurally impossible. Plan selection writes to the same table the cron reads, end of story. <strong>(2) InvoiceRow TZ rendering</strong>: the period label on each invoice row was rendering the UTC month boundary through the browser&rsquo;s local timezone, so May 1 UTC (<code>2026-05-01T00:00:00Z</code>) shifted back one day in any negative-offset locale and the label read &ldquo;April 2026&rdquo; in Mountain Time. Fix: added <code>timeZone: &quot;UTC&quot;</code> to <code>toLocaleString</code> so the label matches the period the row actually covers. Three-line fix on the format options object. <strong>(3) Stale copy cleanup</strong>: the active-plan banner&rsquo;s sub-line used to say &ldquo;Stripe linkage in v366.x &middot; invoices stay in draft until then&rdquo; &mdash; that copy was written before v1.6 wired the actual Stripe linkage. Now reads the truthful state via the <code>pm.hasCardOnFile</code> signal already available on the page: &ldquo;Card on file &middot; invoices charge automatically&rdquo; or &ldquo;No card on file yet &middot; invoices stay in draft until added.&rdquo; Touched: <code>src/routes/app.billing.tsx</code> (9 surgical edits across imports, PLAN_META, state types, pickPlan signature, plan iteration array, PlanCard prop type, planSummary signature, InvoiceRow rendering, active-plan banner copy), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
